0.0012757980730384588,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.0019345632754266262,-7.152555099310121e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-0.02657397650182247,-0.18493086099624634,-1.2170608043670654,-7.510157047363464e-06,-4.410734163684538e-06,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0,-2.0265558760002023e-06,-2.3841855067985307e-07,-5.638440416078083e-05,-3.576272320060525e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,1655,279,5313,13957,287,58184,11,1052,525,2326,7263,315,3040,4217,1817,13,4636,279,58184,525,916,11,279,1602,88188,13026,1817,26025,6078,2326,3039,448,1449,4462,315,279,30222,7263,11,323,3055,448,1817,4462,315,862,1828,2083,382,4340,1657,1424,927,2050,525,1052,304,2790,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nAt the national curling championships, there are three teams of four players each. After the championships are over, the very courteous participants each shake hands three times with every member of the opposing teams, and once with each member of their own team.\n\nHow many handshakes are there in total?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"47aca86e8d24e6ba46c66855df64feae12dbc8627d5feeca5888c9ec3945bcd3"},"seconds":24.62996196746826,"seed":479682838906783434,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve this problem, we need to break it down into two parts:\n\n1. Handshakes between players from different teams.\n2. Handshakes between players from the same team.\n\nLet's start with the first part:\n\n1. **Handshakes between players from different teams:**\n\nSince each team has 4 players, and there are 3 teams, we have a total of \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) players. Each player shakes hands three times with every member of the opposing teams. There are 2 opposing teams, and each opposing team has 4 players, so each player shakes hands with \\(2 \\times 4 = 8\\) players, but only three times with each of these players.\n\nThus, the number of handshakes per player with players from other teams is \\(3 \\times 8 = 24\\).\n\nSince there are 12 players in total:\n\\[ 12 \\times 24 = 288 \\]\n\nHowever, each handshake is counted twice (once for each participant), so the actual number of unique handshakes is:\n\\[ \\frac{288}{2} = 144 \\]\n\n2. **Handshakes between players from the same team:**\n\nEach player shakes hands once with each of the 3 other players on their team. Thus, within each team, there are:\n\\[ 4 \\times 3 = 12 \\]\nhandshakes per team.\n\nSince there are 3 teams, the total number of intra-team handshakes is:\n\\[ 3 \\times 12 = 36 \\]\n\nSince each handshake is counted once, no division is needed here.\n\n3. **Total number of handshakes:**\n\nAdding the two parts together:\n\\[ 144 + 36 = 180 \\]\n\nThus, the total number of handshakes is:\n\\[ \\boxed{180} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{180}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
